							</div>
		
		<div class="entry-content">

			<p>Last time I described <a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/2013/07/my-learning-elixir-erlang-setup/" title="My Learning Elixir (erlang) Setup">my setup for learning Elixir</a>, the language built on top of Erlang with a Ruby bent.  Today I wanted to get a hang of processes and mailboxes which are so important to both languages.  To do this I chose the Triangle Kata as my background story.  <a href="https://gist.github.com/cromwellryan/6024862">Take a look</a>:</p>
<p><script src="https://gist.github.com/cromwellryan/6024862.js"></script></p>
<p><strong>Update:</strong> You might wonder what that <code>slow</code> function is all about.  I added that in there to clarify the parallelism.  You would expect the slowest classifications to appears at the end of the resultant list.</p>
